1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,210
Do you realize
this is probably

2
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:03,587
the last time we're
all going to be here

3
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:06,381
in the coffee house
as six single people.

4
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:08,592
Why, what's happening
to the coffee house?

5
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:13,012
Oh... okay.

6
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,389
Yep, from now on
it's going to be

7
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:16,517
the four of you guys,
and me and the missus.

8
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:18,477
The little woman,
the wife,

9
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,521
the old ball and chain.

10
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:21,814
Ha, old?

11
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:24,023
The young, hot
ball and chain.

12
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,442
That's much better.

13
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:27,319
Oh, we got to go.
Where are you guys going?

14
00:00:27,361 --> 00:00:28,654
We're going to pick up
the wedding dress,

15
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:29,905
then we're going
to have lunch with Mom.

16
00:00:29,947 --> 00:00:31,866
Oh... Joey, you're

17
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:33,074
having lunch with my mom?

18
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,576
No, I just heard "lunch."

19
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:36,912
But, yeah, I can go, sure.

20
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:43,460
You know, actually,
I'm kind of glad
they're leaving

21
00:00:43,502 --> 00:00:47,088
'cause I need to talk
to you about something.

22
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,549
What's up?

23
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,634
Well, this may be
a little awkward...

24
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:52,845
Listen, if you
want to borrow money,
it's kind of a bad time.

25
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:55,681
I'm buying dinner
for 128 people tomorrow night.

26
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:57,725
It's not that.

27
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:00,602
Um, now, what
I'm going to say to you

28
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:02,730
I'm not saying
as your friend, okay?

29
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,106
I'm saying it as
Monica's older brother.

30
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,358
But you're still my friend.

31
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,944
Not for the next few minutes.

32
00:01:08,986 --> 00:01:12,322
During this time,
are you still my best man?

33
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:14,324
Nope.

34
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:16,117
Do I still call you Ross?

35
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:19,204
Okay...

36
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,998
You guys are getting
married tomorrow

37
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:24,501
and-and I couldn't be more
thrilled for both of you.

38
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:26,921
But as Monica's older brother

39
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:28,422
I have to tell you this:

40
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:34,386
If you ever hurt
my little sister...

41
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:36,513
if you ever cause her

42
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:40,059
any unhappiness of any kind,

43
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,728
I will hunt you down

44
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:44,980
and kick your ass.

45
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:48,817
( laughing )

46
00:01:51,904 --> 00:01:53,321
What? I'm serious.

47
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:59,286
Hey, dude, stop it, okay?
I'm not kidding, here.

48
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:01,580
Hey, I hear what
you're saying, okay?

49
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:04,416
And thanks for the warning.

50
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:06,710
No problem.

51
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:09,504
So are we friends again?

52
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:11,590
Yeah.
Okay.

53
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:14,468
You won't believe what Monica's
older brother just said to me.

54
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:26,605
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

55
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:29,024
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

56
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:31,401
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

57
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:36,073
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

58
00:02:36,115 --> 00:02:38,325
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

59
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:41,620
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

60
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:44,957
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

61
00:02:44,999 --> 00:02:48,376
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

62
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,384
Whatcha doing, Mon?

63
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:58,428
I'm making a list
of all the things

64
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:01,306
that are most likely
to go wrong at the wedding.

65
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,392
That way I can be prepared.

66
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:06,812
What are they?
Well, so far I have:

67
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:08,856
my bridesmaids' dresses
won't get picked up,

68
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,398
my veil gets lost,

69
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,651
or I don't have
my "something blue."

70
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:16,446
Hey, those are all the things
that I'm responsible for.

71
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:18,197
I had to go with the odds, Rach.

72
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:20,575
Hey, you guys!

73
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,577
Remember that audition
I had awhile ago

74
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,578
and I didn't get the part?

75
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:24,705
The commercial?
No.

76
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:25,706
That play?
No.

77
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,457
That other play?
No.

78
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:28,458
The movie?

79
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,085
Yes!
Ooh!

80
00:03:30,127 --> 00:03:32,295
The one about the pilot
and his dog who flies planes.

81
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,757
No, no, but, man,
that one hurt. Yeah.

82
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:37,300
No, this is the one
about the soldiers

83
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:38,468
who fight in World War I.

84
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,054
Oh, yeah, mm-hmm.

85
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:44,141
Back then, you know,
we called it The Great War.

86
00:03:44,183 --> 00:03:47,310
It really was.

87
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:49,270
Well, anyway,
the guy they wanted backed out

88
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,313
and now they want me.

89
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,356
I start shooting today!

90
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:52,607
Congratulations!

91
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:53,817
Wait, you can't
start today.

92
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,069
Today is the
rehearsal dinner.

93
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,611
Oh, no, I'll be done by then.

94
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,321
Oh, well, then, way to go,
you big movie star!

95
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:00,741
I know. All right, I'll see
you guys over there.

96
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:02,367
I'm off to fight the Nazis.

97
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:03,702
Oh, wait, Joey!

98
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:05,495
We fought the Nazis
in World War II

99
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:06,914
not World War I.

100
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,498
Whoa, okay.

101
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:11,210
Who was in World War I?

102
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,090
Go ahead.

103
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:17,674
You're going to be late,
go, go!

104
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:18,800
Yeah, see you!

105
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:24,223
Who did we fight
in World War I?

106
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,558
Mexico?
Yes, very good.

107
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,810
Of course.

108
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:43,909
Hey, Joey,
we're ready.

109
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:45,702
Yeah, me, too.

110
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:47,621
Richard, we're
ready for you.

111
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,123
Joey Tribbiani.

112
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:51,250
This is Richard Crosby.
He's playing Vincent.

113
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,044
I'm doing my scenes with you?

114
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:55,545
Nice to meet you, Joey.

115
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:56,964
Wow, I can't believe this.

116
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:58,048
This is incredible.

117
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,759
I mean, you just won an Oscar.

118
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:03,095
No, I didn't.

119
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:04,638
I think you did.

120
00:05:05,889 --> 00:05:08,809
I think I lost, three times.

121
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,603
Uh, um, cookie, would you...

122
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:16,275
Okay, we're about
an hour away

123
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:17,692
from getting
the scene lit

124
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,486
so, uh, if you
guys don't mind

125
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:20,487
can we run it
a couple of times?

126
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,613
Yeah, sure.

127
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:24,116
Okay, all right,
let's do it.

128
00:05:24,158 --> 00:05:25,117
( clearing throat )

129
00:05:25,159 --> 00:05:27,828
And... action!

130
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:29,746
We have to find
the rest of the platoon.

131
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:31,623
Forget the platoon,
the platoon is gone!

132
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:36,335
What?

133
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:37,671
The platoon is dead.

134
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,840
Face facts, Tony.

135
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,383
So what are we going to do?

136
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,303
We have no reinforcements,
no food.

137
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:45,846
No, we still have
food in the basement.

138
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,222
I saw potatoes
and some dry pasta.

139
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,475
Hang on a minute.

140
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:53,061
Joey, you keep
touching your face.

141
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:55,272
Is something wrong?

142
00:05:55,314 --> 00:05:57,398
No, no...

143
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,651
I, uh, I thought it might be

144
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:01,862
kind of a cool
character thing, you know?

145
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:04,656
He's a-- he's a face-toucher.

146
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:08,035
( no audio )

147
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,828
I don't think so.

148
00:06:11,412 --> 00:06:14,499
Let's take it back
to Richard's last line.

149
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,959
Action!

150
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:17,376
We may not have any weapons

151
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,670
but we still have
food in the basement.

152
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:20,964
I saw potatoes
and some dry pasta

153
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:22,299
and a few tins of tuna.

154
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:27,179
Honey, we got to go!

155
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:29,388
Okay, here's a question

156
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:30,724
you never want
to have to ask.

157
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,267
My dad just called
and wanted to know

158
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:35,645
if he could borrow one
of your pearl necklaces.

159
00:06:35,687 --> 00:06:38,899
Did he say what kind
of neckline he'd be wearing?

160
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,608
No.

161
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,735
Well, I've only met him once

162
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:44,321
but I'm guessing "plunging."

163
00:06:44,363 --> 00:06:46,740
Yeah, he is more of
a "if you got it, flaunt it"

164
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:49,076
kind of... father.

165
00:06:50,285 --> 00:06:51,370
I don't have
anything like that

166
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:53,247
but let me go see
if Rachel does.

167
00:06:53,288 --> 00:06:54,789
Yes, include
more people in this.

168
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,418
Hey, do you realize
that at this time tomorrow

169
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,046
we're going
to be getting married?

170
00:07:01,088 --> 00:07:04,423
Wait a minute,
I have a date tomorrow night.

171
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:06,843
I just, I can't
believe that we made it.

172
00:07:06,885 --> 00:07:08,762
Well, you don't have to sound
so surprised.

173
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,764
I'm sorry, but...

174
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,307
Nothing.

175
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:14,809
What?

176
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:17,436
Well, honestly

177
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:19,438
ever since we got engaged,
I've been waiting

178
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,441
for something to flip you out.

179
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:24,778
Honestly... me, too.

180
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:25,862
Really?

181
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,239
Yeah, you know,
I keep thinking

182
00:07:27,281 --> 00:07:28,698
that something stupid
is going to come up

183
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:32,953
and I'll go all...
well, Chandler.

184
00:07:32,994 --> 00:07:34,037
But nothing has.

185
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,496
Oh, I'm so glad.

186
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:38,417
Thank you so much for
staying so calm during this.

187
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:40,835
I mean, it's really,
it's made me stay calm.

188
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:43,297
I could have been worse.

189
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:44,464
Okay.

190
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:46,341
I'll be right there.

191
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:52,806
( phone ringing )

192
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:55,309
MONICA:
Hi, if you're calling
before Saturday

193
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:57,144
you've reached
Monica and Chandler.

194
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:59,020
But if you're calling
after Saturday

195
00:07:59,062 --> 00:08:02,149
you've reached
Mr. and Mrs. Bing!

196
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:05,110
Please leave a message
for the Bings!

197
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,338
Hey, Maureen, hi!

198
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:26,965
Gosh, Chandler,
this is my cousin Maureen.

199
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:28,883
We're the Bings.

200
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,555
Hi, oh, you guys
look so beautiful.

201
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,641
Mr. and Mrs. Bing.

202
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,562
Wow, Monica...

203
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:42,897
Hey, just so you know

204
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,650
I had my "older brother
talk" with Chandler.

205
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:47,194
What is that?

206
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:50,738
Well, I told him that
if he ever hurt you

207
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:54,575
I would hunt him down
and kick his ass.

208
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,577
( laughter )

209
00:08:56,619 --> 00:09:00,165
What, what is the matter
with everybody?

210
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:02,625
I'm serious,
I would kick his ass.

211
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,461
( screaming laughter )

212
00:09:04,503 --> 00:09:07,339
Oh, Ross,
please, my makeup!

213
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,550
Hi...
Chandler!

214
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:13,011
...Mom.

215
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:15,763
Thanks for wearing...
something.

216
00:09:17,474 --> 00:09:19,518
Oh, honey, this
is so exciting.

217
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,478
I thought we'd screwed
you up so bad

218
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,937
this day would never come.

219
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:25,899
And just think--

220
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,069
soon there'll be
lots of little Bings.

221
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,616
I can't believe I have to go
back to work after this

222
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:36,826
and get spit on again.

223
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:38,328
Well, you're lucky.

224
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:41,248
At least the people
that spit on you are famous.

225
00:09:42,332 --> 00:09:43,624
Who spits on you?

226
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:45,293
I don't want to
talk about work.

227
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:50,298
Mrs. Bing,
these are my parents

228
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,883
Judy and Jack Geller.

229
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:53,593
It's lovely to meet you.

230
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:56,388
So, are you his mother
or his father?

231
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:58,348
Jack!

232
00:09:58,390 --> 00:10:01,226
What, I've never
seen one before.

233
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,728
Dad, there's Ross.
Why don't you go talk to him?

234
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:07,190
I didn't even have a chance to
act as though I'm okay with it.

235
00:10:10,569 --> 00:10:12,779
Hello, all.

236
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,615
Hi, Dad.

237
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,617
Hi, Mr. Bing.

238
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:21,955
Nora.

239
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:23,582
Charles.

240
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:28,086
It's so great
to see you both here.

241
00:10:28,128 --> 00:10:29,337
Yes.

242
00:10:29,379 --> 00:10:30,547
Although I think
we may be seeing

243
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:32,591
a little too much
of some people.

244
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:38,637
Aren't you a little old
to be wearing a dress like that?

245
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,723
Don't you have
a little too much penis

246
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,934
to be wearing
a dress like that?

247
00:10:44,561 --> 00:10:46,396
Oh, my God.

248
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:51,651
Of course you can
kick his ass, son.

249
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:55,113
You could kick anyone's ass
you want to.

250
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,283
Thanks, you guys.

251
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:03,204
Oh, Rach, Rach...

252
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:04,498
Hey, could you
do me a favor

253
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:05,957
and would you talk
to Chandler's dad

254
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:07,917
and try to keep him
away from Chandler's mom?

255
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:09,794
Yeah, but I don't know
what he looks like.

256
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,588
He is the man
in the black dress.

257
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:12,880
Man in the black...

258
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:20,180
Oh...

259
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:21,764
Hi, I'm Rachel.

260
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:23,766
I'm a friend of
Monica and Chandler's.

261
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:25,101
I'm Amanda.

262
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:27,187
Oh, I get it.

263
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:29,606
A-man-duh!

264
00:11:29,648 --> 00:11:30,898
